## Mobile rules (iOS Safari and Chrome are both WebKit; desktop devtools emulation hides these bugs)
- Never unscoped `html { scroll-behavior: smooth }`: iOS ignores `window.scrollTo` while it is on. Scope it:
  `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) { html:focus-within { scroll-behavior: smooth } }`.
- `<ScrollToTop>` on route change: set `documentElement.style.scrollBehavior = "auto"`, wait one
  `requestAnimationFrame`, write `window.scrollTo(0,0)`, `documentElement.scrollTop = 0` and `body.scrollTop = 0`,
  restore. `useEffect`, not `useLayoutEffect`. Mobile nav links close and scroll synchronously inside `onClick`.
- `viewport: { viewportFit: "cover" }`; fixed bottom bars use `padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`.
- `min-h-svh` / `h-dvh`, never `min-h-screen` / `100vh`.
- Tap targets ≥ 44×44px; `touch-action: manipulation` on primary buttons; real `<button>`/`<a>` only.
- Inputs/selects/textareas ≥ 16px (or iOS zooms on focus); right `type`/`inputMode`; native `<select>` on mobile.

